window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-6be952b78a5da779"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"set-up-and-manage-chatgpt-in-slack-and-microsoft-teams\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"slack-microsoft-teams-chatgpt\">在 Slack 和 Microsoft Teams 中设置和管理 @ChatGPT</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面网址末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在受支持的 Slack 和 Microsoft Teams 对话中，用户可以请 @ChatGPT 总结信息、起草回复或使用已批准的工具。</p> <p>日常使用说明请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001537\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">帮助中心用户指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>ChatGPT 管理员负责连接平台并配置使用界面、<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420?anchor=step-2-manage-capabilities\">插件</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">工作区连接</a>。Slack 和 Teams 管理员负责设置消息平台。</p> <p>详细设置步骤请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">帮助中心设置指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-access-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">访问权限如何生效</h2> <p>选择 @ChatGPT 服务账户可以使用哪些插件和工作区连接。能使用该界面的人员也能访问这些工具和数据；其范围可能与用户个人权限不同。</p> <p>@ChatGPT 使用已配置的连接和对话上下文，但不会继承个人的文件、应用或私有频道访问权限。在支持的情况下，<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=how-permissions-and-data-sharing-work\">个人插件访问权限</a>需要单独授权。共享回复对该对话的参与者可见。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h2> <p>开始设置前，请确定要连接的 ChatGPT 工作区、Slack 工作区或 Microsoft Teams 租户。确认你的组织可以使用 @ChatGPT，并确定试点用户范围。</p> <p>设置前请分配以下职责：</p> <ul> <li>ChatGPT 工作区管理员或所有者：连接平台、创建界面，并选择其插件和工作区连接。</li> <li>Slack 或 Teams 管理员：批准权限并安装应用。Teams 管理员还要管理受众分配，并与具备相应权限的 Microsoft 管理员协调完成所需的授权审批。</li> <li><strong>连接负责人：</strong> 准备已批准的公司账户，并验证其资源访问权限和操作权限。请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">工作区连接指南</a>进行授权。</li> <li><strong>试点负责人：</strong> 确定要测试的用户范围和支持的对话类型，包括不应拥有访问权限的用户。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"set-up-slack\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"slack\">设置 Slack</h2> <p><span id=\"1-confirm-the-slack-workspace-and-permissions\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"1-plan-your-surface-configuration\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1\">1. 规划界面配置</h3> <p>界面决定 @ChatGPT 可以在哪些位置使用，以及可以使用哪些工具。</p> <p>每个 Slack 工作区都应配置一个界面；Enterprise Grid 中连接的每个工作区也都需要单独配置。</p> <p><a id=\"2-connect-slack-in-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2-chatgpt-slack\">2. 在 ChatGPT 中连接 Slack</h3> <p>在 <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI 管理控制台（需联网）</a>中，选择目标工作区并打开 Agents 以连接 Slack。请审核所请求的权限。</p> <p>让 Slack 所有者或获授权的应用管理员完成所需审批，然后在 ChatGPT 中确认连接。</p> <p>如果组织已经在 Slack 中使用 ChatGPT，Slack 管理员必须批准额外的应用权限，才能使用新版 @ChatGPT 体验。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001536\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">现有 Slack 安装说明（需联网）</a>。新功能发布后，现有安装不会立即停止工作。</p> <p><span id=\"3-create-the-deployment-and-choose-its-scope\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"set-destination-controls-and-instructions\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"3-create-the-surface-and-choose-its-scope\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3\">3. 创建界面并选择范围</h3> <p>为已连接的 Slack 工作区创建界面，并为其取一个容易识别的名称。</p> <p>如果要在频道中开展试点，请选择 <strong>仅限选定频道</strong>，然后添加已批准的频道。此设置不会阻止直接消息。</p> <p><a id=\"4-test-the-experience\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4\">4. 测试使用体验</h3> <p>添加公司连接之前，请先在已批准的 Slack 频道和直接消息中测试请求。</p> <p>如果 @ChatGPT 没有回复，或一分钟内没有显示正在处理，请参照下方的<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=h.no5mkx5zlseo\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">设置故障排查（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-microsoft-teams\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"microsoft-teams\">设置 Microsoft Teams</h2> <p>Microsoft Teams 管理员负责管理应用安装、用户访问权限和任何所需的 Microsoft 许可同意。ChatGPT 工作区管理员负责管理 Teams 连接、界面设置和<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">工作区连接</a>。</p> <p>分步设置说明请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">帮助中心设置指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"check-your-surface-scope\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">检查界面范围</h2> <p>确认界面对应正确的 Slack 工作区或 Teams 租户。Enterprise Grid 中每个已连接的工作区都需要一个界面。</p> <p><span id=\"enable-the-credential-for-the-deployment\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"configure-company-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">配置公司访问权限</h2> <p>请将公司管理的访问权限与个人授权分开处理：</p> <ol> <li><strong>个人访问：</strong> 在支持的情况下，使用 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT.com（需联网）</a>或桌面应用中连接的插件，需要单独授权。这与公司共享访问权限相互独立。</li> <li> <p><strong>公司共享访问：</strong> 界面插件使用所配置公司账户的权限；这些权限可能与对话参与者的个人权限不同。成员不需要逐人登录共享账户。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查界面所连接的 Slack 工作区或 Teams 租户。</p> </li> <li>请连接负责人验证已批准的公司账户权限。设置和授权请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">工作区连接指南</a>。</li> <li>添加已批准的插件，并选择目标工作区连接。</li> <li>保存设置，然后请试点负责人在相应 Slack 或 Teams 对话中测试连接。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"enable-codex-cloud-for-slack\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"slack-codex-cloud\">为 Slack 启用 Codex Cloud</h2> <p>在可用时，从 Slack 委派任务到 Codex Cloud 需要单独设置。</p> <ol> <li>为你的工作区启用 <strong>Codex Cloud</strong>。</li> <li>若适用 <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=review-codex-cloud-access-and-environment-administration\">Codex Cloud 基于角色的访问控制</a>，请授权 Slack 界面的服务账户和发起请求的用户使用该功能。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">发布云环境并与工作区共享</a>。</li> <li>验证每位请求用户对该环境以及任何需要身份验证的代码仓库的访问权限。</li> <li>请试点用户在 Slack 中请求调查某个代码仓库，并确认编码任务已启动。</li> </ol> <p>服务账户负责查找环境；编码任务则以请求用户的身份运行。服务账户不需要 GitHub 访问权限。</p> <p><span id=\"verify-a-pilot-before-expanding-access\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"validate-setup\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">验证设置</h2> <p>扩大访问范围前，请使用已批准的测试数据，检查每种受支持对话类型的请求是否成功，以及访问边界是否正确。</p> <ul> <li><strong>Slack：</strong> 测试一个已批准频道、一个未纳入的频道和直接消息。频道限制不会阻止直接消息。</li> <li>Teams：测试已分配和未分配的用户。只有在界面支持个人聊天时，才测试个人聊天。</li> <li><strong>连接和操作：</strong> 验证执行操作的账户、源数据访问权限，以及已启用的写入或发送操作在已批准目标位置中的结果。</li> <li><strong>回复可见性：</strong> 确认哪些用户能查看回复，以及能否打开链接的来源或文件。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"maintain-the-surface\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">维护界面</h2> <p>指定负责人维护平台连接、应用分配和已批准的插件。遇到安装或许可同意变更时，请联系平台管理员；需要重新授权时，请联系连接负责人。</p> <p>更改权限或连接后，扩大范围前应重复相关<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=h.ts4i3qduozr\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">验证检查（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">工作区连接指南</a>检查公司账户访问权限并排查授权问题。</p> <p>停用或移除访问权限前，请先识别受影响的界面和连接，并与相关管理员协调。</p> <p><span id=\"why-cant-a-teammate-open-a-generated-file\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"why-did-a-working-connection-stop-working\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"what-should-i-include-in-a-support-request\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"what-else-should-we-confirm-before-enabling-chatgpt\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"setup-faq\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">设置常见问题</h2> <p><a id=\"chatgpt\"></a> <strong>为什么有人找不到 @ChatGPT，或收不到回复？</strong></p> <p>对于 Slack 界面：</p> <ul> <li>确认测试所用 Slack 工作区中已安装 @<strong>ChatGPT</strong>。</li> <li>检查频道是否属于该界面连接的 Slack 工作区。</li> <li>请 Slack 管理员在<a href=\"https://slack.com/marketplace/A097V82EGG2-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用详情页（需联网）</a>检查必需的权限范围。</li> </ul> <p>对于 Teams 界面：</p> <ul> <li>确认 Microsoft Teams 管理员已为你的租户启用 @ChatGPT。</li> <li>确认应用已分配给目标用户，并通过已批准的安装方式添加到你正在测试的团队。详细说明请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">帮助中心设置指南（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>确认已为你正在测试的 Teams 租户创建 ChatGPT 界面。</li> </ul> <p><strong>为什么看不到公司信息？</strong></p> <p>检查界面的插件，以及源系统中<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=troubleshoot-access\">已连接账户的访问权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"slack-teams\"></a> <strong>Slack 和 Teams 支持相同的功能吗？</strong></p> <p>不同平台支持的对话类型和功能可能不同。请查看<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001537\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">帮助中心用户指南（需联网）</a>，并测试计划使用的每种工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"chatgpt-1\"></a> <strong>@ChatGPT 如何使用记忆？</strong></p> <p>在功能发布初期，@ChatGPT 不包含记忆功能，也不会使用用户的 ChatGPT 记忆。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"set-up-and-manage-chatgpt-in-slack-and-microsoft-teams\">Set up and manage @ChatGPT in Slack and Microsoft Teams</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>In supported Slack and Microsoft Teams conversations, people can ask @ChatGPT to summarize information, draft responses, or use approved tools.</p> <p>For everyday use, see the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001537\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Help Center user guide (online)</a>.</p> <p>ChatGPT admins connect platforms and configure surfaces, <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420?anchor=step-2-manage-capabilities\">plugins</a>, and <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">workspace connections</a>. Slack and Teams admins manage the messaging-platform setup.</p> <p>For detailed setup, see the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Help Center setup guide (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"how-access-works\">How access works</h2> <p>Choose which plugins and workspace connections @ChatGPT’s service account can use. People who can use the surface can access those tools and data, which may differ from their personal access.</p> <p>@ChatGPT uses configured connections and conversation context. It does not inherit a person’s file, app, or private-channel access. <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=how-permissions-and-data-sharing-work\">Personal plugin access</a> requires separate authorization where supported. Shared replies are visible to conversation participants.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h2> <p>Before setup, identify the ChatGPT workspace and Slack workspaces or Microsoft Teams tenant you intend to connect. Confirm that @ChatGPT is available for your organization and agree on the pilot audience.</p> <p>Assign the following responsibilities before setup:</p> <ul> <li> <p>ChatGPT workspace admin or owner: Connect the platform, create the surface, and choose its plugins and workspace connections.</p> </li> <li> <p>Slack or Teams admin: Approve permissions and install the app. Teams admins also manage audience assignment and coordinate required consent with an authorized Microsoft administrator.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Connection owner:</strong> Prepare approved company accounts and verify their resource and action permissions. Follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">Workspace connections guide</a> for authorization.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Pilot owner:</strong> Define the audience and supported conversations to test, including people who should not have access.</p> </li> </ul> <h2 id=\"set-up-slack\">Set up Slack</h2> <p><span id=\"1-confirm-the-slack-workspace-and-permissions\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"1-plan-your-surface-configuration\">1. Plan your surface configuration</h3> <p>A surface defines where @ChatGPT is available and which tools it can use.</p> <p>Configure one surface per Slack workspace, including each connected workspace in Enterprise Grid.</p> <h3 id=\"2-connect-slack-in-chatgpt\">2. Connect Slack in ChatGPT</h3> <p>In the <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI admin console (online)</a>, select the intended workspace and open Agents to connect Slack. Review the requested permissions.</p> <p>Have the Slack owner or authorized app manager complete any required approval, then confirm the connection in ChatGPT.</p> <p>If your organization already uses ChatGPT in Slack, a Slack admin must approve the additional app permissions to use the new @ChatGPT experience. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001536\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">guidance for existing Slack installations (online)</a>. Existing installations won’t stop working immediately at launch.</p> <p><span id=\"3-create-the-deployment-and-choose-its-scope\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"set-destination-controls-and-instructions\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"3-create-the-surface-and-choose-its-scope\">3. Create the surface and choose its scope</h3> <p>Create a surface for the connected Slack workspace and give it a recognizable name.</p> <p>For a channel pilot, choose <strong>Selected channels only</strong> and add the approved channels. This does not block direct messages.</p> <h3 id=\"4-test-the-experience\">4. Test the experience</h3> <p>Before adding company connections, test a request in an approved Slack channel and in a direct message.</p> <p>If @ChatGPT does not respond or show that it is working within a minute, follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=h.no5mkx5zlseo\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">setup troubleshooting checks (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> below.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-microsoft-teams\">Set up Microsoft Teams</h2> <p>Microsoft Teams admins manage app installation, user access, and any required Microsoft consent. ChatGPT workspace admins manage the Teams connection, surface settings, and <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">workspace connections</a>.</p> <p>For step-by-step setup instructions, see the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Help Center setup guide (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"check-your-surface-scope\">Check your surface scope</h2> <p>Confirm the surface matches its Slack workspace or Teams tenant. Enterprise Grid needs one surface per connected workspace.</p> <p><span id=\"enable-the-credential-for-the-deployment\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"configure-company-access\">Configure company access</h2> <p>Keep company-managed access separate from personal authorization:</p> <ol> <li> <p><strong>Personal access:</strong> Where supported, using plugins connected in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT.com (online)</a> or the desktop app requires separate authorization. This is separate from shared company access.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Shared company access:</strong> Surface plugins use the configured company account’s permissions, which may differ from participants’ personal access. Members do not each authenticate the shared account.</p> </li> <li> <p>Check the surface’s connected Slack workspace or Teams tenant.</p> </li> <li> <p>Have the connection owner verify the approved company account’s permissions. Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=create-a-workspace-connection\">Workspace connections guide</a> for setup and authorization.</p> </li> <li> <p>Add the approved plugin and select the intended workspace connection.</p> </li> <li> <p>Save, then have the pilot owner test the connection in its Slack or Teams conversation.</p> </li> </ol> <h2 id=\"enable-codex-cloud-for-slack\">Enable Codex Cloud for Slack</h2> <p>Codex Cloud delegation from Slack requires separate setup where available.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Enable <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> for your workspace.</p> </li> <li> <p>Where <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=review-codex-cloud-access-and-environment-administration\">Codex Cloud role-based access control</a> applies, grant access to the Slack surface’s service account and requesting users.</p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">Publish a cloud environment and share it with your workspace</a>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Verify each requesting user’s access to the environment and any repositories requiring authentication.</p> </li> <li> <p>Have a pilot user request a repository investigation in Slack and confirm the coding task starts.</p> </li> </ol> <p>The service account finds environments; the coding task runs as the requesting user. The service account does not need GitHub access.</p> <p><span id=\"verify-a-pilot-before-expanding-access\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"validate-setup\">Validate setup</h2> <p>Before expanding access, use approved test data to check successful requests and access boundaries for each supported conversation type.</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>Slack:</strong> Test an approved channel, an excluded channel, and direct messages. Channel restrictions do not block direct messages.</p> </li> <li> <p>Teams: Test assigned and unassigned users. Test personal chat only where your surface supports it.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Connections and actions:</strong> Verify the acting account, source access, and results of enabled write or send actions in approved destinations.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Reply visibility:</strong> Confirm who can see responses and open linked sources or files.</p> </li> </ul> <h2 id=\"maintain-the-surface\">Maintain the surface</h2> <p>Assign an owner to maintain platform connections, app assignment, and approved plugins. Involve platform admins for installation or consent changes and connection owners for reauthorization.</p> <p>After a permission or connection change, repeat the relevant <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=h.ts4i3qduozr\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">validation checks (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> before expanding access. Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">Workspace connections guide</a> to review company-account access and troubleshoot authorization.</p> <p>Before offboarding or removing access, identify affected surfaces and connections and coordinate with their administrators.</p> <p><span id=\"why-cant-a-teammate-open-a-generated-file\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"why-did-a-working-connection-stop-working\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"what-should-i-include-in-a-support-request\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"what-else-should-we-confirm-before-enabling-chatgpt\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"setup-faq\">Setup FAQ</h2> <p><a id=\"why-cant-people-find-chatgpt-or-get-a-response\"></a> <strong>Why can’t people find @ChatGPT or get a response?</strong></p> <p>For Slack surfaces:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Confirm that @<strong>ChatGPT</strong> is installed in the Slack workspace you are testing.</p> </li> <li> <p>Check that the channel belongs to the surface’s connected Slack workspace.</p> </li> <li> <p>Have a Slack admin check required scopes on the <a href=\"https://slack.com/marketplace/A097V82EGG2-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">app details page (online)</a>.</p> </li> </ul> <p>For Teams surfaces:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Confirm that a Microsoft Teams admin has enabled @ChatGPT for your tenant.</p> </li> <li> <p>Confirm that the app is assigned to the intended users and added to the team where you are testing through the approved installation route. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Help Center setup guide (online)</a> for detailed instructions.</p> </li> <li> <p>Confirm a ChatGPT surface exists for the Teams tenant you are testing.</p> </li> </ul> <p><a id=\"why-is-company-information-missing\"></a> <strong>Why is company information missing?</strong></p> <p>Check the surface’s plugins and the <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=troubleshoot-access\">connected account’s access</a> in the source system.</p> <p><a id=\"do-slack-and-teams-support-the-same-features\"></a> <strong>Do Slack and Teams support the same features?</strong></p> <p>Conversation types and features can differ between platforms. Check the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001537\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Help Center user guide (online)</a> and test each planned workflow.</p> <p><a id=\"how-does-chatgpt-interact-with-memory\"></a> <strong>How does @ChatGPT interact with memory?</strong></p> <p>At launch, @ChatGPT does not include memory or use a person’s ChatGPT memories.</p>"};
